/**
 * @page topic_winget WinGet package
 *
 * @brief Installing ascii-chat with Windows Package Manager.
 *
 * The Windows release publishes an x64 WiX MSI. The release workflow can
 * generate a manifest for the exact MSI, calculate its SHA-256, and open a
 * pull request in the publisher's fork of Microsoft's
 * [winget-pkgs repository](https://github.com/microsoft/winget-pkgs).
 *
 * To enable the automated submission, create a fork named `winget-pkgs` under
 * the publisher account, then add a repository secret named
 * `WINGET_GITHUB_TOKEN`. The token needs permission to push to that fork and
 * open pull requests against `microsoft/winget-pkgs`. Optionally set the
 * `WINGET_FORK_REPOSITORY` repository variable if the fork is under another
 * account.
 *
 * After Microsoft's manifest review merges the initial submission, users can
 * install and update ascii-chat with:
 *
 * @code{.ps1}
 * winget install ascii-chat
 * winget upgrade ascii-chat
 * @endcode
 *
 * The WinGet package is the runtime application only. The development ZIP and
 * ARM64 portable ZIP remain available from the GitHub release page.
 */
